From a515273731d5ad3efc897f8ed92baea9a74b7bb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Velle Sinclair <brncomputerhelp@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:54:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/28] fix(data): read wallpaper JSON with comments and
 trailing commas

Wallpaper Engine's own reader accepts both, and its content relies on
it: the stock effects/fluidsimulation/effect.json and
presets/water/preset.json close a list with a trailing comma, and stock
effect files carry commented-out keys. nlohmann rejects both, so any
wallpaper using the fluid simulation effect failed to load with "parse
error at line 403, column 2" (workshop 2901183422 bundles a copy; issue
#396 is the same failure).

parseLenient drops comments and trailing commas outside strings, keeps
newlines so parse errors still name the file's own line, and is used
wherever a wallpaper's files are read: project.json, scene, model,
material, effect, particle and texture metadata. The engine's own config
file and shader annotations stay strict.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
